    "accession": "PXD013063",
    "title": "HeLa Cells Cross-Linked In Vivo versus as a Lysate",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "HeLa Cells were cross-linked with PIR either in vivo or as a lysate.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Cells used for intact cross-linking were immediately mixed with BDP-NHP to a final concentration of 10mM, incubated while shaking at room temperature (hereafter RT) for 30 minutes, and then washed with ammonium bicarbonate until pellet was no longer yellow.  Cell samples used for lysate cross-linking were first snap frozen in liquid nitrogen and then stored at -80℃ until they were cryoground at -80℃ with Retsch MM 400 cryomill.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "5 fraction runs were cobined separately for the in vivo and lysate cross-linked samples.  Data was analyzed with Mango and searched with Comet.",
